WEBVTT

00:21.060 --> 00:22.540
What's wrong? What happened?!

00:37.140 --> 00:44.860
Spice and Wolf

01:55.450 --> 01:57.510
I said I was sorry...

01:57.510 --> 02:02.930
Of course, I am happy to give you 
some warmth in this cold.

01:57.680 --> 02:01.680
<b>Episode 20
Church Girl and Miller Boy</b>

02:03.460 --> 02:06.210
That is why I have turned 
a blind eye to your actions

02:06.210 --> 02:08.140
and refrained from demanding any payment.

02:08.140 --> 02:10.260
Even so, Lawrence.

02:10.260 --> 02:12.650
Are there not things you must never do?!

02:12.990 --> 02:15.150
This tail of mine is my pride.

02:15.550 --> 02:18.150
The sole proof of who I am.

02:18.940 --> 02:20.150
And my tail...

02:21.660 --> 02:27.620
had its hairs pulled out 
and flattened! Moreover...

02:34.460 --> 02:37.950
How dare you fall asleep!

02:54.010 --> 02:55.680
We should be able to see the town soon.

02:55.680 --> 02:58.650
Is that where we can ask about my home town?

02:58.930 --> 03:05.240
Ms. Diana told me that there's an abbot who 
collects various stories of pagan gods there.

03:05.240 --> 03:06.080
I see.

03:06.080 --> 03:08.870
So, this abbot lives in that town.

03:08.870 --> 03:12.330
No, the abbey is in a very secluded place.

03:12.330 --> 03:15.500
The only one who knows its whereabouts
is a church priest in Tereo.

03:15.500 --> 03:17.920
So, we are going to Tereo.

03:17.920 --> 03:21.970
No. Since we don't know how to get to Tereo,

03:21.970 --> 03:24.150
we need to stop by the town 
of Enberch to get directions.

03:25.940 --> 03:28.390
What a roundabout path.

03:36.680 --> 03:40.330
You are very lucky 
to live in the town of Enberch.

03:40.330 --> 03:45.260
That's because God always stands 
beside those who are properly faithful.

03:44.110 --> 03:45.780
I wish to eat sweet bread.

03:45.780 --> 03:48.430
After we sell our goods.

03:45.780 --> 03:48.570
You, who are being taught 
the true way by the official Church,

03:48.430 --> 03:50.340
Remind me what goods we carry this time?

03:48.570 --> 03:50.090
have no reason not to be blessed.

03:50.340 --> 03:54.180
You remember, right? It's flour 
that we bought from Marc in Kumerson.

03:54.180 --> 03:57.250
Oh. Right, right. It was flour.

03:57.550 --> 03:59.850
This is also my first time visiting this town.

03:59.850 --> 04:02.880
I didn't know what kind of 
products were in demand.

04:02.880 --> 04:03.720
Even so...

04:04.060 --> 04:06.610
I thought a town of this size 
would have rich nobles

04:06.610 --> 04:09.220
or a large church that would buy some.

04:09.220 --> 04:11.580
I put at least a little thought 
into the purchase.

04:11.580 --> 04:14.230
I do not care about such shallow cleverness.

04:14.740 --> 04:21.240
Why must I eat black and bitter rye bread 
every day when we carry such goods in our cart?

04:24.000 --> 04:27.620
Though you made a lot of money 
in Kumerson, you are still quite stingy!

04:27.620 --> 04:29.050
Hey, now...

04:29.050 --> 04:32.400
We're not on this journey 
just to find your home town.

04:32.400 --> 04:34.430
We're also here for my trade!

04:34.430 --> 04:35.500
Fool!

04:35.500 --> 04:39.000
My cute tail was beaten by your legs!

04:39.000 --> 04:43.210
It is not fair unless 
I can beat your arse in return!

04:43.210 --> 04:45.360
No more rye bread!

04:45.360 --> 04:49.640
I wish to eat soft and fluffy wheat bread!

04:49.640 --> 04:52.210
There was a bountiful harvest of rye this year.

04:52.210 --> 04:55.060
We don't have the extra 
finances to deal with wheat.

04:55.060 --> 04:59.770
Wheat is profitable, so we 
wish we could buy it from you...

04:59.770 --> 05:04.440
I wish we could have 
sold you bread instead of flour.

05:05.400 --> 05:07.690
That is how all merchants think.

05:07.690 --> 05:09.910
But then, you'd be picking 
a fight with the bakeries.

05:10.240 --> 05:12.160
Are the bakeries powerful here?

05:12.160 --> 05:13.500
Very powerful!

05:13.500 --> 05:15.090
If anyone other than a bakery bakes bread,

05:15.090 --> 05:17.640
they'd come after you with stone rolling pins.

05:17.640 --> 05:20.460
Are you looking to create 
a sales channel this time?

05:20.720 --> 05:24.410
No, I'm just trading as I travel.

05:24.410 --> 05:26.640
Where is your destination?

05:26.640 --> 05:28.650
I plan to head to Lenos.

05:28.650 --> 05:31.360
Lenos? That far?

05:31.360 --> 05:34.810
Before that, I wish to stop by Tereo.

05:34.810 --> 05:36.730
I have some business with their church.

05:37.350 --> 05:41.770
Tereo's church? The church 
in Enberch is much grander...

05:41.770 --> 05:44.370
Oh yes, you have a large church here.

05:44.370 --> 05:47.870
Our church manages this entire area.

05:47.870 --> 05:51.140
We have an extraordinary priest 
named Father Mendez, too...

05:51.140 --> 05:55.260
Oh, no. I just want to meet 
someone from Tereo's church.

05:55.260 --> 06:00.000
Oh, by the way, do you know 
how to get to Tereo?

06:00.000 --> 06:02.960
There's a direct road, so you won't get lost.

06:02.960 --> 06:06.090
It's about a day's travel from here by cart.

06:06.090 --> 06:07.470
Thank you very much.

06:08.070 --> 06:09.930
May God bring us together in the future.

06:09.930 --> 06:13.620
Yes, I hope we do business 
together at that time.

06:13.620 --> 06:16.270
Hey, it seems Tereo is only a day away.

06:16.270 --> 06:16.850
Huh?

06:16.850 --> 06:17.850
Yeah, it seems so.

06:18.270 --> 06:21.270
If we depart today, we should 
be able to reach it by the morrow.

06:21.540 --> 06:24.940
Shouldn't we rest? Aren't you tired?

06:24.940 --> 06:28.100
We can rest in Tereo tomorrow.

06:28.100 --> 06:30.650
I would like to go as soon as possible.

06:30.650 --> 06:31.780
All right.

06:31.780 --> 06:34.240
Let's eat something warm before we go.

06:34.240 --> 06:35.830
We can at least do that, right?

06:37.300 --> 06:38.910
Well, of course.

07:11.930 --> 07:13.410
What is that sound?

07:13.410 --> 07:14.380
It's from that.

07:21.920 --> 07:24.670
Since there's a waterwheel, we must be close.

07:34.970 --> 07:36.470
Whoa, there.

07:38.530 --> 07:39.840
Sorry. Sorry.

07:39.840 --> 07:41.520
Say, aren't you a traveler?

07:42.580 --> 07:44.570
That's right. Who are you?

07:45.590 --> 07:47.490
As you can see, I'm a miller.

07:47.490 --> 07:50.530
So, where'd you come from? 
You don't look like you're from Enberch.

07:50.800 --> 07:53.300
You have a good eye. Let me ask you back.

07:53.300 --> 07:55.820
How much longer 
till we reach the town of Tereo?

07:55.820 --> 07:57.340
The "town" of Tereo?

07:57.340 --> 07:59.790
If Tereo is a town, 
then Enberch is a royal capital.

08:00.240 --> 08:02.790
I don't know why you're going,
 but it's a tiny village.

08:03.250 --> 08:05.760
I see. So, how much further?

08:05.760 --> 08:07.400
It's just a bit further down the road.

08:07.400 --> 08:09.930
You could even say you're already in Tereo.

08:09.930 --> 08:11.930
I see. I understand, thank you.

08:11.930 --> 08:15.680
H-Hey, there! There's no rush! Right, traveler?

08:17.060 --> 08:18.350
Do you have some business with me?

08:18.350 --> 08:22.060
Oh, um, business?

08:22.060 --> 08:25.350
Oh, th-that's right! You have 
quite a beauty by your side.

08:28.360 --> 08:30.250
She's a nun in the middle of a pilgrimage.

08:30.250 --> 08:31.850
A nun?

08:31.850 --> 08:33.070
Is there a problem?

08:33.070 --> 08:37.570
Well, it's not a good idea 
to bring a nun into Tereo.

08:37.870 --> 08:38.700
Oh?

08:39.220 --> 08:42.210
We have business with the church in Tereo.

08:42.210 --> 08:45.330
It shouldn't be a problem 
for a nun to visit a church.

08:45.330 --> 08:47.930
W-Well, how should I put this,

08:47.930 --> 08:52.920
there's a fight going on with the annoying 
people from the Church of Enberch.

08:53.310 --> 08:57.420
Won't things get complicated 
if a traveling nun gets involved?

08:57.420 --> 09:00.360
I see. Well, we'll be careful.

09:00.360 --> 09:03.810
No one would mind if we visited as long 
as she isn't dressed as a nun, right?

09:04.440 --> 09:06.710
That would be great.

09:06.710 --> 09:08.810
But what business do you have with the church?

09:08.810 --> 09:10.370
We came to ask for directions.

09:10.370 --> 09:11.230
Directions?

09:12.630 --> 09:15.420
So, you didn't come here to do business.

09:15.420 --> 09:17.860
I was hoping to help if you were.

09:18.170 --> 09:19.530
I'll come to you if that happens.

09:19.530 --> 09:20.370
May I pass now?

09:31.980 --> 09:34.010
My name is Kraft Lawrence.

09:34.290 --> 09:35.610
What's yours?

09:35.610 --> 09:36.380
Evan!

09:36.380 --> 09:38.090
Gyoam Evan!

09:38.090 --> 09:41.510
Evan. Got it. I'll remember your name.

09:41.510 --> 09:43.890
Yeah, don't forget it!

09:45.890 --> 09:48.900
Please stop by on your way out, too!

10:05.390 --> 10:07.620
His eyes were more on you than me.

10:07.620 --> 10:09.290
Well, he's a miller.

10:09.290 --> 10:10.800
He probably doesn't have an easy life.

10:10.800 --> 10:11.840
Is that so?

10:11.840 --> 10:14.190
It's like being a shepherd.

10:14.190 --> 10:17.450
It's a necessary job, but a lot of 
towns and villages don't like them.

10:18.300 --> 10:20.900
You have wheat in that pouch, right?

10:20.900 --> 10:22.910
If you were to hull and grind that much wheat,

10:22.910 --> 10:24.720
how much do flour do you think it'll yield?

10:24.720 --> 10:29.060
I was just a god of harvest. 
I do not know such a thing.

10:29.060 --> 10:32.060
Let's say you have this much grain.

10:32.400 --> 10:36.190
If you hull it and grind it into flour, 
you'll have about this much at the end.

10:36.190 --> 10:38.800
That little?

10:39.700 --> 10:44.760
They say that millers at the waterwheel 
always steal some of the flour. {Note: Literal translation, he has an extra hidden finger that steals the wheat.}

10:44.760 --> 10:47.700
Also, waterwheels are usually 
owned by the landlord.

10:47.700 --> 10:51.810
Who do you think collects the taxes from 
everyone who grinds their wheat there?

10:51.810 --> 10:53.960
I assume it would be the miller.

10:53.960 --> 10:54.960
That's right.

10:54.960 --> 10:57.090
Nobody pays their taxes happily.

10:57.630 --> 10:59.550
So, who do they end up hating?

11:01.170 --> 11:02.220
I see.

11:02.620 --> 11:05.640
Then, the reason that whelp 
was wagging his tail at you...

11:05.640 --> 11:09.350
Yes, he's probably dying to find 
a way to leave this village.

11:09.660 --> 11:12.940
There has to be someone running the grinder,

11:12.940 --> 11:17.440
but most people are suspicious of them 
and hate them. It's a thankless job.

11:18.150 --> 11:20.440
A familiar story to me...

11:21.620 --> 11:23.910
But it's a necessary job.

11:25.730 --> 11:27.490
There are people who appreciate it, too.

11:58.720 --> 12:00.900
What a large stone.

12:00.900 --> 12:06.410
It's probably used for festival ceremonies, 
dancing, or holding meetings.

12:06.980 --> 12:09.370
Hello. Nice to meet you.

12:59.720 --> 13:00.920
Who is it?

13:00.920 --> 13:03.370
I apologize for the sudden visit.

13:03.370 --> 13:06.220
I am a traveling merchant named Lawrence.

13:06.220 --> 13:07.930
A traveling merchant?

13:07.930 --> 13:10.380
Yes, I came from Kumerson.

13:10.870 --> 13:11.680
And, who is she?

13:12.120 --> 13:14.940
Due to some circumstances, 
she is currently traveling with me.

13:21.970 --> 13:23.820
What business do you have here?

13:23.820 --> 13:28.360
I'd like to meet with 
the priest of this church.

13:28.360 --> 13:30.580
I am not an official priest, but...

13:33.800 --> 13:37.540
My name is Elsa Schtingheim, 
and I am responsible for this church.

13:37.540 --> 13:38.520
Huh?

13:38.520 --> 13:40.420
So, what business do you have?

13:40.420 --> 13:42.930
W-We came to ask for directions.

13:42.930 --> 13:43.720
Directions?

13:43.720 --> 13:46.550
I am looking for the directions 
to Diendran Abbey.

13:46.880 --> 13:50.800
The abbot, Louis Lana Schtinghilt, 
should be caring for it.

13:51.630 --> 13:52.790
I do not know!

13:55.100 --> 13:58.840
I heard there was a priest 
named Father Franz here.

13:59.190 --> 14:01.470
Father Franz passed away last summer!

14:01.470 --> 14:01.860
Huh?

14:01.860 --> 14:02.940
Are you satisfied now?!

14:02.940 --> 14:06.860
I don't know about the abbey 
you speak of and I'm very busy!

14:07.290 --> 14:08.600
R-Right...

14:10.980 --> 14:12.740
She really disliked you.

14:13.150 --> 14:15.260
Is it because I didn't give a donation?

14:16.370 --> 14:19.700
Is it true that Father Franz is dead?

14:19.700 --> 14:22.200
She doesn't seem to be lying. However...

14:22.200 --> 14:22.750
Yeah.

14:23.240 --> 14:25.720
She's definitely lying about 
not knowing about the abbey.

14:30.170 --> 14:32.160
It has been so long...

14:32.160 --> 14:35.340
It's a pretty small village. 
Don't cause any problems.

14:36.350 --> 14:38.850
That will depend on your attitude.

14:41.300 --> 14:42.800
I am a bit sleepy.

14:42.800 --> 14:43.860
May I sleep?

14:44.390 --> 14:46.530
What if I say no?

14:47.050 --> 14:49.740
I will just doze off at your side.

14:53.490 --> 14:56.320
Well, I know you're really tired.

14:56.320 --> 14:58.510
As my traveling companion, 
I would appreciate you resting

14:58.510 --> 15:00.080
before getting sick from exhaustion.

15:00.330 --> 15:03.530
Yes. Then, I shall rest now.

15:03.530 --> 15:05.680
Before that, you should take off your robe,

15:05.680 --> 15:08.460
fold my coat that you just tossed aside,

15:08.460 --> 15:10.760
and properly rest under the blankets.

15:13.260 --> 15:16.720
If the clothes aren't folded properly 
by the time I come back,

15:17.380 --> 15:19.270
your dinner will drop in quality.

15:19.270 --> 15:22.230
I know you are too kind to do such a thing.

15:22.230 --> 15:25.550
You'll get yourself hurt one of these days.

15:25.550 --> 15:27.970
Only if you do something about it.

15:27.970 --> 15:29.580
Where are you going now?

15:29.580 --> 15:32.110
Since it looks like we're 
going to stay here a bit,

15:32.110 --> 15:34.190
I want to go and greet the head of the village.

15:34.190 --> 15:37.080
I may be able to ask him about the abbey, too.

15:38.660 --> 15:41.140
So, be obedient and sleep.

15:42.500 --> 15:43.460
Yes...

15:44.090 --> 15:45.640
I won't have any gifts for you, though.

15:46.420 --> 15:47.380
I do not mind.

15:49.580 --> 15:52.130
All I ask is that you return.

15:53.250 --> 15:55.880
That foolish face of yours is enough of a gift.

15:57.070 --> 15:58.650
I've already received my gift.

15:59.270 --> 16:00.640
Good night.

16:02.490 --> 16:04.150
Sleep well.

16:23.860 --> 16:25.110
Is anyone home?

16:25.890 --> 16:27.040
Coming.

16:28.550 --> 16:30.460
Yes, yes. Who is it?

16:30.770 --> 16:34.060
I apologize for the sudden visit. 
I'm a traveling merchant...

16:34.060 --> 16:34.980
Oh, my!

16:34.980 --> 16:38.060
Elder! It's the rumored man!

16:38.060 --> 16:39.810
Elder!

16:41.080 --> 16:42.810
See, here he is!

16:42.810 --> 16:46.570
Ms. Kemp, you're being rude to our guest.

16:46.570 --> 16:47.850
Yes, yes.

16:47.850 --> 16:50.320
Please forgive our terrible manners.

16:51.500 --> 16:55.820
I am the head of Tereo Village. My name is Sem.

16:58.860 --> 17:00.660
Were you in the middle of something?

17:00.660 --> 17:01.810
No, no.

17:01.810 --> 17:05.980
We're in the middle of turning 
the wheat we harvested into bread.

17:15.150 --> 17:18.170
Please be at ease. It isn't alive.

17:18.700 --> 17:19.890
It's stuffed?

17:21.080 --> 17:21.890
Now then.

17:22.290 --> 17:25.350
What business do you have here?

17:25.350 --> 17:28.240
First, I wanted to give you my regards.

17:28.240 --> 17:30.860
This is some of the wheat flour 
I have brought with me.

17:30.860 --> 17:32.320
Goodness!

17:32.320 --> 17:37.620
Lately, business is the first word 
out of other traveling merchants.

17:37.620 --> 17:39.800
And, your second goal?

17:39.800 --> 17:44.750
I am looking for an abbey.

17:44.750 --> 17:49.310
I asked about its whereabouts 
at the church earlier, but they didn't know.

17:49.310 --> 17:50.840
Is that so?

17:51.130 --> 17:54.720
I know of no abbey in this area...

17:54.720 --> 17:58.470
I heard that Father Franz 
would know the location of the abbey.

17:58.470 --> 18:01.310
Father Franz passed away last summer.

18:01.310 --> 18:02.610
I heard.

18:02.610 --> 18:04.770
We lost a good man.

18:05.650 --> 18:10.190
He devoted many years 
of his life to this village.

18:12.170 --> 18:14.570
Has Ms. Elsa taken his place?

18:14.830 --> 18:18.450
Yes. She's quite young, 
so I'm sure you were surprised.

18:18.450 --> 18:20.090
Yes. So, then—

18:21.450 --> 18:22.620
Elder!

18:22.620 --> 18:24.740
It seems something has happened.

18:25.020 --> 18:27.250
It's always busy right after the harvest.

18:27.550 --> 18:29.790
I'm sorry I couldn't do more for you...

18:29.790 --> 18:30.900
Elder!

18:32.880 --> 18:35.020
I was told to bring this here!

18:35.880 --> 18:38.880
Sorry it took so long! The roads were...

18:51.020 --> 18:53.020
I should get some sleep myself.

19:07.450 --> 19:09.870
I recall you said the quality 
of dinner would drop

19:09.870 --> 19:12.030
if the clothes were not folded 
and I was not under the covers?

19:12.030 --> 19:15.450
You're too kind to do something like that.

19:18.540 --> 19:20.050
I must have slept a long time.

19:20.050 --> 19:25.680
Was I not so kind that I did not wake you 
even though my stomach rumbled?

19:25.680 --> 19:29.200
So, you didn't sadly sneak 
the coins out of my purse?

19:34.050 --> 19:36.020
It seems night falls quickly here.

19:36.020 --> 19:38.150
There is no one in the square.

19:38.150 --> 19:42.010
No stalls, either. 
Will we be able to find dinner?

19:42.010 --> 19:43.930
I'm sure we'll be fine at the tavern.

19:43.930 --> 19:45.740
Yes. Then, let us hurry.

19:46.540 --> 19:48.120
I just woke up...

19:50.030 --> 19:52.430
Okay. I got it...

19:53.500 --> 19:54.540
What's that?

20:05.010 --> 20:07.760
Don't pop out like that. That surprised me.

20:08.680 --> 20:10.330
What is he doing?

20:10.330 --> 20:11.890
Seems like he's heading toward the church.

20:12.250 --> 20:13.750
How suspicious.

20:17.870 --> 20:19.510
We're definitely more suspicious.

20:26.090 --> 20:27.750
I see...

20:30.250 --> 20:33.830
Only gods are allowed to peek 
into the lives of people.

20:35.220 --> 20:37.170
Are you not interested?

20:38.370 --> 20:41.460
I'm surprised you'd be 
so interested in such gossip.

20:41.460 --> 20:43.970
What is wrong with being interested?

20:43.970 --> 20:45.950
It's hardly praiseworthy behavior.

20:46.830 --> 20:51.120
I am not only interested 
because of mere curiosity.

20:52.520 --> 20:55.230
I would rather call it studying.

20:55.230 --> 20:56.440
Studying?

20:56.440 --> 20:58.320
Yes. Studying.

20:58.320 --> 21:03.110
To study how you and I would 
look in the eyes of others.

21:06.790 --> 21:10.030
Is it not necessary to see things 
from another perspective?

21:14.910 --> 21:19.380
So, that is how it looks 
when others see me with you.

21:25.310 --> 21:28.720
Well, I do not think 
we pale in comparison to them.

21:29.210 --> 21:30.930
Right, Lawrence?

21:35.640 --> 21:37.100
Hey, you.

21:40.290 --> 21:41.650
Are you listening?

21:46.610 --> 21:47.860
I am hungry.

21:54.760 --> 21:55.800
You're right.

21:55.800 --> 21:58.690
We should get some food 
and gather some information.

21:58.690 --> 22:01.520
Yes, we must seek out 
the location of the abbey.

22:01.520 --> 22:03.800
No, I'm going to change how we go about this.

22:03.800 --> 22:04.980
Oh?

22:04.980 --> 22:09.550
I think Elsa and Sem both know about the abbey.

22:09.550 --> 22:11.800
Even so, they're pretending that they don't.

22:12.100 --> 22:14.010
So, I'm going to look into why first.

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Episode 21

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Pagan Village and Priest's Contract

23:45.830 --> 23:49.230
Next Episode: 
Pagan Village and Priest's Contract
